      "path": "ForServer/tests/transport_tests.cpp",
      "content": "The three-second check does not bound this test: EXPECT_EQ continues on timeout, and download.get() then waits indefinitely if the worker is stuck waiting for HANDLE_CLOSING. Early assertion exits also wait in the std::async future destructor, before SocketOwner closes the stalled connection. No CTest timeout is configured for this target. Add a process-level watchdog/CTest timeout and arrange failure cleanup to cancel and close the server sockets before joining; replacing EXPECT_EQ with ASSERT_EQ alone will not avoid the future-destructor wait.",
